<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anyang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anyang is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, near the site of Yin, the last capital of the Shang dynasty. Excavations there since 1928 have uncovered royal tombs, palace foundations and tens of thousands of inscribed oracle bones, the earliest Chinese writing. The ruins of Yin became a World Heritage Site in 2006.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anyang.jpg" alt="Anyang" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Windmemories · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20250831_Temple_of_Han_Qi_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
